# Workflow Safety Router

Canon: `AGENTS.md` § Delivery safety. Detail: `documents/agent-workflows/workflow-safety.md`.

## Core rule

Dirty root is **user state**, not cleanup debt. Report it; protect it; **never auto-fix** (stash, restore, clean, checkout).

## Default policy

```text
Review-only first → local patch → single working branch → PR on explicit command only
```

| Forbidden by default | Exception |
|----------------------|-----------|
| branch, PR create/push | explicit "create branch" / "open PR" |
| all `git clean` variants (`-fd`, `-fdX`, `-fxd`, …) | explicit approval + preview + targeted cache path only |
| `git reset --hard` | explicit approval |
| untracked delete, branch delete | explicit approval |
| auto `stash apply` / `stash pop` | explicit approval |
| `git checkout` / `git switch` Mode 0–1 | explicit branch-move request |
| dirty files **outside** task scope | user approves continue, narrow scope, or review-only |

## Modes

| Mode | Scope | Git |
|------|-------|-----|
| 0 Review | design, patch plan | no edits; no checkout/switch/clean/stash/commit/branch |
| 1 Local patch | 1–3 files; scope ⊆ dirty OK | current branch only; no checkout/switch |
| 2 Single branch | multi-commit slice | one `work/*` branch; create/switch only to it |
| 3 Real PR | merge-ready | tests pass; scope-clean; explicit "open PR" |

Default **Mode 1** (local patch) when user provides plan/spec or says "auto". Mode 0 (review-only) only when user explicitly asked for review only.

## Before first edit

1. `git status --short` — report dirty files.
2. Dirty **outside** explicit scope → if user explicitly scoped the task, proceed with narrow scope (user has already decided). If task is **unscoped** or user said "auto", check only critical paths (git, secrets, CI).
3. All dirty inside scope → Mode 1 may proceed on current branch.
4. Edit only scoped paths.
5. Protected — never wholesale delete: `plans/**`, `documents/**`, `documents/**`, `var/plan-run/**`, `.worktrees/**`, `.devtool/**`. `graphify-out/**`: hybrid — see detail doc.

## Slice naming

**Step 1 / Step 2 / …** = implementation sequence. "PR1/PR2" = slice size, not mandatory GitHub PRs.

## Integration

`git-worktree.mdc`, `ops-recovery.mdc`, `AGENTS.md` § Default workflow step 7.
